{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{# Shadow of Skyrim: what the speaker knows about the player's defeat.
   SkyrimNet records the player's death as an ordinary death event, and Battle Summaries
   narrates the fight. Neither says what Shadow of Skyrim did next: the player did not stay
   dead, they woke somewhere else, and their gear is gone. That is the gap this block fills.

   The signal is the persisted death event for the player, read from event history. It is
   NOT the nemesis tracker quests: those are started by script only when a nemesis is
   assigned, and a solo defeat by two wolves started none of them. Verified in game - a real
   defeat started 0 of 5 nemesis trackers and 0 of 5 gear trackers. A death event, by
   contrast, is written for every defeat and survives the respawn.

   The 21600-second (6 game hour) window matches Battle Summaries' own game_hours setting,
   so the two agree on what counts as recent. Without it the death event would sit in
   history forever and this block would claim a defeat the player suffered days ago.

   The count is 200, not 40, because it is a RECENCY budget, not a match count: a busy
   player generates roughly 30 events per game hour, so 40 would reach back only ~80
   minutes and a defeat older than that would never be seen. 200 covers the full 6-hour
   window with headroom. Measured against a real save: the death event sat 167 events deep
   in the player's own history, far past a 40-event horizon.

   is_knocked_down covers the live moment, while the player is still on the ground. It is
   checked first and separately, because during bleedout the death event has not been
   written yet, and after respawn the knockdown is already over.

   This file ADDS a block; it replaces no SkyrimNet prompt. It is inert without Shadow of Skyrim. #}
{% if is_plugin_loaded("Shadow of Skyrim.esp") %}

{% set wasDefeated = false %}
{% for e in get_recent_events(200, player.UUID) %}
{% if e.type == "death" and existsIn(e.data, "victim") and e.data.victim == player.name and (gameTimeNumeric - e.gameTime) < 21600 %}{% set wasDefeated = true %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if is_knocked_down(player.UUID) %}
**{{ player.name }} IS DOWN:**
- {{ player.name }} has been struck down and is bleeding out on the ground right now - unable to act, unable to answer.
- The fight is not decided yet. Whoever is still standing decides what happens next.
{% else %}
{% if wasDefeated %}
**{{ player.name }} WAS DEFEATED:**
- {{ player.name }} was struck down in a fight and did not win it. They are on their feet again, but not because they fought their way out.
- Shadow of Skyrim does not let a defeat kill. {{ player.name }} woke somewhere other than where they fell - however far the victor carried them.
- Gear, gold, or both may have been taken. If a nemesis claimed the victory, that creature is still out there wearing what it took.
- {{ player.name }} knows this happened. Do not act as though they simply walked away from that fight, and do not invent a victory for them.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
